[MEDIUM] The rest of the 17 journaled security findings are adopted and verified:
- every SEMAPHORED and SEM_EXECUTE operation is a trigger, including UVM's ACQ_CIRC_GEQ with ACQUIRE_SWITCH_TSG (uvm_turing_host.c:53-70);
- SET_MEMORY_SCRUB_PARAMETERS is address-free (channel_utils.c:675-676);
- SET_SECURE_COPY_MODE and the CC address methods are refused; stock uses them only under confidential computing (uvm_hopper_ce.c:545, :588);
- SubDeviceMask is refused by name, not classified;
- SET_OBJECT, PHYS_MODE and MEM_OP A-C are authored;
- TSpace is a distinct type, never in Mirrors;
- the per-twin state is a CAS word, with Kernel sticky and reset on recycle (mem.rs:2156);
- the USERD bound is off+USERD_SIZE inside the usable heap (zero_userd caps at USERD_SIZE, host.rs:462-469);
- a per-launch piece bound;
- the vIOMMU seam is one dma_to_file_range function.
